        "content": {
          "passageId": "english-pre-a1-m018-reading-passage-01",
          "passage": "There are four seasons in the year. In spring, flowers grow and the trees have new leaves. Summer is often sunny and warm. In autumn, leaves turn brown and fall to the ground. Winter is cold, and sometimes we see snow. The sun shines in every season, but the weather changes. I like spring because the garden is full of flowers."
        },
